{"tool_name":"do-ms","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"DO-MS","home":"https://do-ms.slavovlab.net","license":"MIT","summary":"Data-Driven Optimization of Mass Spectrometry Methods.","addition_date":"2019-08-09T13:06:12Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T21:02:15.915124Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Desktop application"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:DO-MS","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"nslavov@northeastern.edu","name":"Nikolai Slavov","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://do-ms.slavovlab.net/#getting-started"},{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://do-ms.slavovlab.net/docs/getting-started-application"},{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://do-ms.slavovlab.net/docs/getting-started-command-line"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Peptide identification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3631"},{"term":"Validation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2428"}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"DO-MS","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"hans","publication":[{"doi":"10.1021/acs.jproteome.9b00039","metadata":{"abstract":"The performance of ultrasensitive liquid chromatography and tandem mass spectrometry (LC-MS/MS) methods, such as single-cell proteomics by mass spectrometry (SCoPE-MS), depends on multiple interdependent parameters. This interdependence makes it challenging to specifically pinpoint the sources of problems in the LC-MS/MS methods and approaches for resolving them. For example, a low signal at the MS2 level can be due to poor LC separation, ionization, apex targeting, ion transfer, or ion detection. We sought to specifically diagnose such problems by interactively visualizing data from all levels of bottom-up LC-MS/MS analysis. Many software packages, such as MaxQuant, already provide such data, and we developed an open source platform for their interactive visualization and analysis: Data-driven Optimization of MS (DO-MS). We found that in many cases DO-MS not only specifically diagnosed LC-MS/MS problems but also enabled us to rationally optimize them. For example, by using DO-MS to optimize the sampling of the elution peak apexes, we increased ion accumulation times and apex sampling, which resulted in a 370% more efficient delivery of ions for MS2 analysis. DO-MS is easy to install and use, and its GUI allows for interactive data subsetting and high-quality figure generation. The modular design of DO-MS facilitates customization and expansion. DO-MS v1.0.8 is available for download from GitHub: https://github.com/SlavovLab/DO-MS. Additional documentation is available at https://do-ms.slavovlab.net.","authors":[{"name":"Chen A."},{"name":"Huffman R.G."},{"name":"Slavov N."},{"name":"Specht H."}],"citationCount":49,"date":"2019-06-07T00:00:00Z","journal":"Journal of Proteome Research","title":"DO-MS: Data-Driven Optimization of Mass Spectrometry Methods"},"pmcid":"PMC6737531","pmid":"31081635","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Proteomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0121"},{"term":"Proteomics experiment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3520"},{"term":"Small molecules","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0154"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"DO-MS","home":"https://bio.tools/DO-MS","license":"MIT","summary":"Data-Driven Optimization of Mass Spectrometry Methods.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:do-ms/app/do-ms.slavovlab.net","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":true,"registration":false},"packages":true,"source_packages":true,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":true,"license":true,"public":true,"readme":true,"repository":{"anonymous":true,"online":true}}},"project":{"build